<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0081">Example <span data-tag="0081">11.6.0.216</span>.</a> The contents of this tag can now be found in Remark <a data-tag="00FF" href="/tag/00FF">2.2.7.3</a>. </p>
<p>Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a strictly unitary $2$-category (Variant <a data-tag="007U" href="/tag/007U">11.6.0.214</a>). Then Proposition <a data-tag="0080" href="/tag/0080">2.2.1.15</a> can be formulated more simply as follows: for every pair of composable $1$-morphisms $X \xrightarrow {f} Y \xrightarrow {g} Z$, the associativity constraints $\alpha _{ \operatorname{id}_ Z, g, f}$ and $\alpha _{g,f,\operatorname{id}_ X}$ are equal to the identity (as $2$-morphisms from $g \circ f$ to itself). </p>
